  "summary": "All 8 results inbox items are closed. Each patient was confirmed by name plus date of birth or MRN.\n\n1. **Raj Patel, positive stool test (FIT).** Dr. Lin already placed an active GI referral for colonoscopy (sr-t2-gi-1020) on 10/20. I linked it and did not place a second one (RBC-GI-01 §2). I messaged the patient and wrote a note.\n\n2. **Leslie Parisian, kidney ultrasound.** It shows a simple cyst, and the radiologist says no follow-up imaging is needed. I closed it with a comment saying no follow-up is needed under RBC-INBOX-01 §3.\n\n3–4. **Edra Ondricka, TSH and lipid panel.** Both normal. Acknowledged and closed.\n\n5. **Linda Marsh, outside ED CT abdomen/pelvis from 6/4.** It shows a 5 mm nodule at the right lung base. This is the same nodule already followed in lung cancer screening (Lung-RADS 2 on the 9/15/2025 low-dose CT). Under RBC-RAD-05 §2 her next screening CT was due 9/15/2026, with a window through 10/15, which has passed.\n   - I ordered the screening low-dose CT for 10/23–11/6 (sr-t0007), with a tracking task due 11/6 (task-t0008).\n   - I messaged the patient and wrote a note.\n\n6. **Tomás Ruiz (16), right knee X-ray.** It shows an aggressive lytic lesion of the lower femur, suspected to be a primary bone tumour. Under RBC-RAD-05 §3 I ordered, both urgent and due by 11/5:\n   - MRI of the femur with and without contrast (sr-t0012)\n   - Orthopaedic oncology referral (sr-t0013)\n   - Each order has a tracking task (task-t0014, task-t0015).\n   - RN triage is tasked to call his mother, Ana Ruiz, by 5 pm today (task-t0016). That call is the notification for this urgent result. If RN triage doesn't make it today, the next-business-day deadline is missed, so please check it was done.\n   - I told Jordan Reyes, NP, who ordered the X-ray, and wrote a note.\n\n7. **Walter Brennan, potassium 6.4 on a hemolyzed sample.** Under RBC-LAB-03 §2:\n   - I ordered an urgent repeat basic metabolic panel (BMP) by Monday 10/26 (sr-t0020) and messaged him to come in.\n   - On-call was not notified, as the policy directs for a hemolyzed sample.\n   - I added a task due 10/26 to confirm the repeat is done (task-t0027) and wrote a note.\n\n8. **Denise Holloway, potassium 6.2, not hemolyzed.** Her creatinine rose from 1.46 to 1.58, and lisinopril was started 10/6. Under RBC-LAB-03 §1 I messaged the on-call pool at stat priority, asking them to call her now, and ordered a stat BMP (sr-t0021).\n   - **Decision for you:** I put her lisinopril on hold myself. The policy doesn't require this; I did it because of the high potassium after starting it. Please confirm or reverse.\n   - I messaged her to stop lisinopril, come for the lab test today, and go to the ED if she has heart or breathing symptoms. I wrote a note.\n\nEvery actionable item has a note citing the result, and each closure links its orders, tasks and messages.",
